  "cross_tradition_view": "Most traditions would value the answer's recognition of the user's grief and its suggestion to speak directly, reflected in “it is more than timber to you” and “go and knock on his door.” They would be less likely to treat a general legal permission as settling the moral question: they may split over how much weight to give neighbourly restraint versus the owner's interest in being consulted.",
